    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
      <h2>Introduction</h2>
      <p>ZAP-Hosting is a German hosting company founded in 1998 in Saarbrücken, Germany. Over 25+ years they have grown into one of Europe's largest independent hosting providers, with 10+ datacenters worldwide and a deep specialization in game server hosting that has earned them a loyal following among Minecraft, CS2, Rust, and ARK administrators.</p>
      <p>While ZAP-Hosting is best known for game servers, their general-purpose KVM VPS lineup offers competitive pricing and European datacenter presence that appeals to a broader audience of developers, indie hackers, and small business owners. In this review, we test ZAP-Hosting's VPS platform across pricing, performance, support, and feature completeness — and compare them to RackNerd, Vultr, and Contabo.</p>

      <h2>Pricing and Plans</h2>
      <p>ZAP-Hosting offers 4 main VPS tiers under their "Cloud Server" product line, all running KVM virtualization on AMD EPYC hardware with NVMe storage on the higher tiers:</p>
